  m_text: J. J. Thomson proposed an early atomic model known as the Thomson Model
    or Plum Pudding Model. In this model, the atom was described as a sphere of positive
    charge spread uniformly throughout its volume, with negatively charged electrons
    embedded within it. The model did not include a central nucleus. The total positive
    charge balanced the total negative charge of the electrons, making the atom electrically
    neutral.
